{
  "$comment": "Campaign level 35, the chapter 3 finale (S4 L7-C). One wide continent shared by four tribes: the player south west (two watchtowers and four posted wardens at home), the western tribe (turtle, easy, a fortified village of eight posted wardens and three towers) north west, the north eastern tribe (aggressive, hard, fortified) and the south eastern tribe (sneaky, hard) behind a high ridge on the player's eastern flank and a sea channel to its north, so it cannot be reached (or reach anyone) until the summit is prayed. A volcano cone fills the centre with the summit Reliquary on its flat top. Ley, ward and seer stones sit at the mountain's feet in rival hands, with wolf dens between. Staged: pray the Heart Stone (the only ley stone) away from the western tribe and hold it three minutes. The hold is contested: from 110 s three fresh western wardens march in every 150 s to kneel and pray it back, and from 180 s the western tribe sends up to four of its own troops on the same beat (both stop once the hold is done); the bot takes the stone near tick 2000, loses it near 4750, retakes it near 8250 and finishes the hold near 11750. Then burn the western Hearth; kill twenty north eastern troops (the stage sends a war band at the village, and fresh bands come every two minutes from 900 s until it is done); pray the summit Reliquary with six followers for Volcano (no rival troops are posted there: the level bot cannot clear guards of a tribe that is already gone); the summit lifts a bridge over the channel, twelve wardens join the player and the last tribes march; then break every tribe. Rivals pray on their own only from 3600 s, so the single use summit cannot be stolen. Idle player: the north eastern bands burn the Hearth near tick 22000 (hearthLost). Bot win near tick 36000.",
